k County District Court\nRural Water\nSocial Sevice SWHHS\nSheriff Office\nTransfer Station\nUniversity Of Minnesota Extension Rock County\nVeterans Service Office\nLand Management Office\nJob Opportunities\nCommunity Links\nCommunity Services\nMinnesota Links\nTownship Officials\nCity Officials\nstart animation start slide 1 of 1\nAshley Kurtz\nAuditor-Treasurer\nOpens in a new tab\n204 E. Brown Street\n507-283-5060\n507-283-1343\nashley.kurtz@rockmn.gov\nRock County Courthouse\nMonday\n8:00AM - 5:00PM\nRelated Pages\nTax Parcel Information\nRock County GIS\nProperty Taxes\nElections\nLicense Center\n2024 Financial Statement\nTax Capacity Rates\nUnderstanding Your Property Taxes\nAuctioneer License\nCity Officials\nTownship Officials\nVendor Payments\nLicense Center\nHome\nDepartment Directory\nAuditor Treasurer\nLicense Center\nDriver's License - Instruction Permit - State ID\nExam Information\nMotor Vehicle Registration & Title Transfers\nDepartment of Natural Resources\nDid you know that if you mail your motor vehicle renewals into the State, the County does not receive any of those fees. Please help keep our office open but taking care of these services right at the Courthouse. You can renew your registration through our office by the following ways:\n1. Visit the License Center from 8:00 am to 5:00 pm Monday through Friday. We currently accept cash, check or credit card.\n2. Mail your renewal form and payment to us at License Center, PO Box 509, Luverne MN 56156.\n3. Drop off your renewal form and payment in our drop box located outside the parking lot entrance to the Courthouse.\nNote: If you are mailing or using the drop box, please make sure to include valid insurance information as well as a good phone number in case we have to contact you with questions.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHow many days do you have to transfer a motor vehicle title?\nYou have 10 days to transfer title on a motor vehicle.\nHow soon do you need to change your address on your driver's license after moving?\nYou have 30 days to change the address on your driver's license.\nHow soon do you need to obtain a driver's license and transfer motor vehicle registrations when moving into Minnesota?\nYou have 60 days after moving into the State to obtain a Minnesota driver's license and Minnesota license plates.\nContact Us\nMon – Fri 8AM – 5PM\nRock County Facebook\nRock County YouTube\nPowered by\nVisit the Revize website (opens in a new tab)\n,\nthe Government Website Experts\nLogin\nShare this page\nShare this page\n-->\nClose\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nSource Language: Target Language: Source Text: Translated Text: Vote:\nClose Read More",
